#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:275
msgid "Shipping a product"
msgstr "分发产物"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:277
msgid ""
"A product is an artifact of the PurRDF build that wrote it, not a stable "
"interchange format. Ship it beside the binary that will restore it — in the "
"same container image, the same release bundle, the same build cache entry — "
"and treat its bytes as a cache key rather than as a document."
msgstr ""
"产物是写出它的那个 PurRDF 构建的工件，而不是稳定的交换格式。应将其与将要恢复"
"它的二进制文件一同分发——在同一个容器镜像、同一个发布包、同一个构建缓存条目中"
"——并把它的字节视为缓存键，而不是文档。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:282
msgid "Two version facts govern whether a restore succeeds:"
msgstr "恢复能否成功，取决于两项版本事实："

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:284
msgid ""
"The **container format version** is refused outright when it is not the one "
"this build decodes. Re-pack with the build that will execute the product."
msgstr ""
"**容器格式版本**不是本构建所解码的版本时，会被直接拒绝。应使用将要执行该产物"
"的构建重新打包。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:286
msgid ""
"The **preparation stage id** is a content-derived digest over the "
"declarative model and the tables its meaning depends on. It is never hand-"
"incremented, so it cannot fall out of step with what the model means. A "
"product carrying a stage id this build does not know is _not_ dead: "
"`rebuild` restores it."
msgstr ""
"**预备阶段 id** 是一个由内容推导出的摘要，涵盖声明式模型及其含义所依赖的各个"
"表。它从不手动递增，因此不可能与模型的含义脱节。携带本构建所不认识的阶段 id "
"的产物*并非*无法使用：`rebuild` 可以恢复它。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:291
msgid ""
"Because the writer is deterministic, a build system can address products by "
"content: pack, hash the bytes, and skip the work when the hash is already "
"present. `purrdf shacl explain` reads a product's own identity digest back "
"out without admitting anything, which is the cheap way to ask \"is this the "
"product for this configuration?\" before deciding to restore it."
msgstr ""
"由于写出器是确定性的，构建系统可以按内容寻址产物：打包、对字节求哈希，并在该"
"哈希已存在时跳过这项工作。`purrdf shacl explain` 会在不准入任何内容的情况下读"
"出产物自身的身份摘要，这是在决定恢复之前询问「这是否就是对应此配置的产物？」"
"的低成本方式。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:297
msgid "Restoring a product"
msgstr "恢复产物"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:303
msgid ""
"`--shapes` and `--shapes-product` are mutually exclusive, and exactly one is "
"required. The verdict is the identical one `--shapes shapes.ttl` reaches: "
"the same engine entry point runs, over the same restored shapes."
msgstr ""
"`--shapes` 与 `--shapes-product` 互斥，且必须恰好提供其中之一。其裁决与 `--"
"shapes shapes.ttl` 得出的裁决完全相同：运行的是同一个引擎入口点，作用于同样恢"
"复出的形状。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:307
msgid ""
"Four flags that describe a shapes **parse** are refused by name against a "
"product rather than accepted and ignored, because that parse does not happen "
"here:"
msgstr ""
"描述形状**解析**的四个标志在与产物同用时会被点名拒绝，而不是被接受后忽略，因"
"为这里不会发生该解析："

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:311
msgid "Flag"
msgstr "标志"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:311
msgid "Why it is refused"
msgstr "拒绝原因"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:311
msgid "Where it belongs"
msgstr "应当使用之处"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:313
msgid "`--shapes-from`"
msgstr "`--shapes-from`"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:313
msgid ""
"names the syntax a shapes document is read as, and a product is not a "
"document"
msgstr "指定形状文档读取时所用的语法，而产物不是文档"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:313
msgid "not applicable"
msgstr "不适用"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:314
msgid "`--shapes-graph`"
msgstr "`--shapes-graph`"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:314
msgid "the product records its own `sh:shapesGraph` IRI"
msgstr "产物记录其自身的 `sh:shapesGraph` IRI"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:314
msgid "pass `--shapes-graph IRI` to `purrdf shacl pack` and re-pack"
msgstr "把 `--shapes-graph IRI` 传给 `purrdf shacl pack` 并重新打包"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:315
msgid "`--import`"
msgstr "`--import`"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:315
msgid "the `owl:imports` closure is folded at pack time"
msgstr "`owl:imports` 闭包在打包时已折叠"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:315
msgid "pass `--import IRI=FILE` to `purrdf shacl pack`"
msgstr "把 `--import IRI=FILE` 传给 `purrdf shacl pack`"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:316
msgid "`--box-role-vocab`"
msgstr "`--box-role-vocab`"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:316
msgid ""
"the product records its own box-role vocabulary (or its deliberate absence)"
msgstr "产物记录其自身的盒角色词汇表（或对其有意的缺省）"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:316
msgid "pass `--box-role-vocab NS` to `purrdf shacl pack` and re-pack"
msgstr "把 `--box-role-vocab NS` 传给 `purrdf shacl pack` 并重新打包"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:318
msgid ""
"Everything describing the **data** graph stays live: `--from`, `--base`, `--"
"format`, the governor flags (`--fuel`, `--deadline`, `--max-intermediate-"
"cells`, `--max-scratch-bytes`, `--max-remote-requests`), and the positional "
"`IN`/`OUT`."
msgstr ""
"描述**数据**图的一切仍然有效：`--from`、`--base`、`--format`、governor（执行"
"调控器）标志（`--fuel`、`--deadline`、`--max-intermediate-cells`、`--max-"
"scratch-bytes`、`--max-remote-requests`），以及位置参数 `IN`/`OUT`。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:323
msgid "Which shapes produced this verdict"
msgstr "哪些形状产生了这一裁决"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:325
msgid ""
"Every `validate` run writes one `shacl shapes-provenance` line to stderr, "
"before the verdict, naming where its shapes came from:"
msgstr ""
"每次 `validate` 运行都会在裁决之前向 stderr 写出一行 `shacl shapes-"
"provenance`，指明其形状的来源："

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:342
msgid ""
"The token is total — there is always one, and none of them means "
"\"unknown\". A restored product renders the artifact's own **input "
"binding**, the same 64 hexadecimal digits `shacl explain` prints on its "
"`identity-digest` line, so a report and the artifact behind it are compared "
"on one spelling:"
msgstr ""
"该标记是完全的（total）——总会有一个，且其中没有任何一个表示「未知」。恢复的产"
"物会呈现该工件自身的**输入绑定**，即 `shacl explain` 在其 `identity-digest` "
"行上打印的同样 64 个十六进制数字，因此报告与其背后的工件是按同一种拼写进行比"
"较的："

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:349
msgid "'/^shacl shapes-provenance restored-/{print $3}'"
msgstr "'/^shacl shapes-provenance restored-/{print $3}'"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:349
msgid "# the artifact\n"
msgstr "# 该工件\n"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:352
msgid ""
"The three tokens are `parsed`, `restored-admitted <digest>` and `restored-"
"rebuilt <digest>`. The two restore tokens stay distinct because the digest "
"means something different on each: **admitted** says the product's binding "
"was checked against this process before anything reached a validator, while "
"**rebuilt** says it was read off the artifact and deliberately _not_ checked "
"— see [`rebuild`, the forward-compatibility path](#binding-a-restore-to-the-"
"product-you-meant) for why checking it there would refuse exactly the "
"products that path rescues."
msgstr ""
"三个标记分别是 `parsed`、`restored-admitted <digest>` 与 `restored-rebuilt "
"<digest>`。两个恢复标记保持区分，因为摘要在二者上的含义不同：**admitted** 表"
"示在任何内容到达验证器之前，产物的绑定已针对本进程进行了检查；而 **rebuilt** "
"表示该摘要是从工件上读出的，并且有意*未*加检查——关于为何在那里检查它会恰好拒"
"绝该路径所要挽救的那些产物，参见[`rebuild`，前向兼容路径](#把恢复绑定到本意所"
"指的产物)。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:361
msgid ""
"This answers the half of the question authentication does not. Admission "
"asks _may this process execute these bytes?_; the provenance line answers "
"_which artifact did this report come out of?_, which is the question a "
"consumer has afterwards, looking at a verdict in a log."
msgstr ""
"这回答了认证所不回答的那一半问题。准入问的是*本进程可以执行这些字节吗？*；溯"
"源行回答的是*这份报告出自哪个工件？*，这正是使用方事后在日志中查看某个裁决时"
"会提出的问题。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:366
msgid "Binding a restore to the product you meant"
msgstr "把恢复绑定到本意所指的产物"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:368
msgid ""
"Every check above asks about **this process** — is this the build that wrote "
"the memo, are these the registries the product was prepared against, is the "
"class analysis the product carries the one its own identity pins. Not one of "
"them asks whether the file named on the command line is the product you "
"wanted, because nothing in a product states which product was meant. So "
"naming the wrong one is not an error:"
msgstr ""
"上面的每项检查问的都是**本进程**——这是否是写出该备忘（memo）的构建，这些是否"
"是产物预备时所针对的注册表，产物携带的类分析是否就是其自身身份所固定的那一"
"份。其中没有一项会问命令行上指定的文件是否就是所需的产物，因为产物中没有任何"
"内容表明本意所指的是哪个产物。因此指定了错误的产物并不是错误："

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:380
msgid ""
"That is a decided, well-formed, authenticated verdict about a shapes graph "
"nobody asked about, and it exits `0`. `--expect-identity HEX` is how you say "
"which product you meant:"
msgstr ""
"这是关于一个无人问及的形状图的、已判定的、良构的、经过认证的裁决，并且以 `0` "
"退出。`--expect-identity HEX` 就是用来说明本意所指产物的方式："

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:393
msgid ""
"`HEX` is the product's **input binding**: the 64 hexadecimal digits of the "
"identity that covers the shapes dataset, the `sh:shapesGraph` IRI, the "
"prefix map, the base, the profile, the box-role vocabulary, all three "
"registries and the class catalog at once. Read it off the product you intend "
"with either verb that prints it — `shacl explain`'s `identity-digest` line, "
"or `shacl verify`'s stdout — and pass it back unchanged:"
msgstr ""
"`HEX` 是产物的**输入绑定**：其身份的 64 个十六进制数字，该身份同时涵盖形状数"
"据集、`sh:shapesGraph` IRI、前缀映射、基准、profile、盒角色词汇表、全部三个注"
"册表以及类目录。可通过任一会打印它的动词从目标产物上读出——`shacl explain` 的 "
"`identity-digest` 行，或 `shacl verify` 的 stdout——并原样传回："

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:401
msgid ""
"$(purrdf shacl explain shapes.purrshp | awk '/^identity-digest /{print $2}')"
msgstr ""
"$(purrdf shacl explain shapes.purrshp | awk '/^identity-digest /{print $2}')"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:402
msgid "\"$WANT\""
msgstr "\"$WANT\""

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:405
msgid ""
"The check is the **first** thing the restore does, ahead of the profile and "
"the stage id: a caller who named the wrong artifact is told that, rather "
"than sent to re-pack a product that was never the one they wanted. It costs "
"a 32-byte comparison, because the identity digest is already decoded by the "
"time the bytes have opened."
msgstr ""
"该检查是恢复所做的**第一**件事，先于 profile 与阶段 id：指定了错误工件的调用"
"方会被如实告知这一点，而不是被引导去重新打包一个从来就不是其所需的产物。其代"
"价是一次 32 字节的比较，因为在字节打开之时，身份摘要就已经解码完毕。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:411
msgid ""
"A satisfied expectation changes nothing else. `--expect-identity` with the "
"product's own digest produces the report byte-identical to the run without "
"the flag — the flag changes the door, not the answer."
msgstr ""
"一个得到满足的期望不会改变其他任何东西。以产物自身的摘要使用 `--expect-"
"identity`，产生的报告与不带该标志运行时逐字节相同——该标志改变的是入口，而不是"
"答案。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:415
msgid ""
"Two spellings are refused as usage errors (exit `2`) rather than accepted: "
"`--expect-identity` against `--shapes`, because a shapes document has no "
"prepared binding to require; and a value that is not 64 hexadecimal digits, "
"which names no dimension because no product was ever inspected. Case is not "
"significant on the way in, so a selector that passed through a manifest or a "
"CI variable in upper case still names its product."
msgstr ""
"有两种写法会作为用法错误被拒绝（退出码 `2`），而不是被接受：对 `--shapes` 使"
"用 `--expect-identity`，因为形状文档没有可供要求的预备绑定；以及不是 64 个十"
"六进制数字的值，这种情况不指明任何维度，因为根本没有检查过任何产物。输入时不"
"区分大小写，因此经由清单或 CI 变量以大写形式传递的选择器仍然指向其产物。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:422
msgid ""
"The writer is byte-deterministic, so the binding is a property of the shapes "
"graph and its parse inputs, not of a particular pack run: re-packing the "
"same shapes graph under the same base and prefixes yields the same digest, "
"which is what makes the selector worth writing down in a deployment manifest "
"beside the product it names."
msgstr ""
"写出器是逐字节确定性的，因此绑定是形状图及其解析输入的属性，而不是某次特定打"
"包运行的属性：在相同的基准与前缀下重新打包同一形状图会得到相同的摘要，这正是"
"该选择器值得与其所指产物一起写入部署清单的原因。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:428
msgid ""
"Under the hood there are two ways a product becomes a validator again, and "
"they are two entry points at one boundary rather than a flag on one:"
msgstr ""
"在底层，产物重新成为验证器有两种方式，它们是同一边界上的两个入口点，而不是某"
"一个入口点上的标志："

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:431
msgid ""
"**`admit`** — the common path. It re-derives nothing expensive: verify the "
"profile, verify the stage id, check the host-supplied registries, restore "
"the dataset, decode the model and the class analysis carried with it, link "
"it, and check the complete input binding — the carried analysis included."
msgstr ""
"**`admit`**——常用路径。它不重新推导任何开销大的内容：验证 profile，验证阶段 "
"id，检查宿主提供的注册表，恢复数据集，解码模型及随之携带的类分析，对其进行链"
"接，并检查完整的输入绑定——包括所携带的分析。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:435
msgid ""
"**`rebuild`** — the forward-compatibility path, taken when the stage id is "
"one this build does not know. It ignores the model section entirely — the "
"carried class analysis with it — and re-derives the shapes, and their "
"analysis, from the dataset the product carries, under the product's own "
"recorded parse inputs. That is what makes it the remedy: a product it must "
"rescue is by definition one whose carried analysis came from a different "
"reachability rule."
msgstr ""
"**`rebuild`**——前向兼容路径，在阶段 id 为本构建所不认识的 id 时采用。它完全忽"
"略模型部分——连同所携带的类分析——并在产物自身记录的解析输入下，从产物携带的数"
"据集重新推导形状及其分析。这正是它能作为补救手段的原因：按定义，它所必须挽救"
"的产物，其携带的分析来自不同的可达性规则。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:442
msgid ""
"Every binding reaches both paths, not only Rust: the CLI's `validate --"
"shapes-product --rebuild`, Python's `ShapesProduct.rebuild()`, the C ABI's "
"`purrdf_shapes_product_rebuild`, and WebAssembly's "
"`shaclProductValidateToSarifRebuild` are the identical two-entry-point seam "
"described here, each restoring the SAME carried dataset `admit` would "
"restore a memo of — so rebuilding a CURRENT product (one whose stage id this "
"build does know) reaches the byte-identical report `admit` does, on every "
"surface. `rebuild` composes with the \"which product did you mean\" "
"expectation too: `--rebuild --expect-identity`, `rebuild_expecting`, and the "
"identical Rust `ShapesProductView::rebuild_expecting` all check the "
"expectation FIRST, exactly as `admit_expecting` does, so re-deriving from "
"the dataset never bypasses the binding a caller required."
msgstr ""
"每种绑定都能到达这两条路径，而不仅仅是 Rust：CLI 的 `validate --shapes-"
"product --rebuild`、Python 的 `ShapesProduct.rebuild()`、C ABI 的 "
"`purrdf_shapes_product_rebuild`，以及 WebAssembly 的 "
"`shaclProductValidateToSarifRebuild`，都是此处描述的同一个双入口点扩展点，每"
"一个恢复的都是 `admit` 会恢复其备忘的那个**同一**携带数据集——因此重建一个**当"
"前**产物（其阶段 id 为本构建所认识）时，在每个接口上都会得到与 `admit` 逐字节"
"相同的报告。`rebuild` 也可以与「本意所指是哪个产物」的期望组合使用：`--"
"rebuild --expect-identity`、`rebuild_expecting`，以及完全相同的 Rust "
"`ShapesProductView::rebuild_expecting`，都会**首先**检查该期望，与 "
"`admit_expecting` 完全一样，因此从数据集重新推导绝不会绕过调用方所要求的绑"
"定。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:455
msgid ""
"**`rebuild` is not a Turtle fallback.** No RDF text is parsed and no file is "
"read; the dataset travels inside the product under the envelope's digests. "
"The alternative — carrying only the compiled model and telling callers to "
"keep the source document for the day the format moves — would make forward "
"compatibility depend on a file the product does not own and cannot "
"authenticate."
msgstr ""
"**`rebuild` 不是 Turtle 后备。** 不解析任何 RDF 文本，也不读取任何文件；数据"
"集在封套摘要的保护下随产物传递。另一种做法——只携带编译后的模型，并告诉调用方"
"为格式变更的那一天保留源文档——会使前向兼容性依赖于一个产物并不拥有、也无法认"
"证的文件。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:463
msgid "// Ask what the bytes are, without admitting them.\n"
msgstr "// 询问这些字节是什么，而不准入它们。\n"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:466
msgid "// Both restore seams consume the view, so re-open to take one.\n"
msgstr "// 两个恢复扩展点都会消耗该视图，因此需重新打开才能使用其中一个。\n"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:474
msgid ""
"// Or state WHICH product you meant, and fail closed when it is not that "
"one.\n"
"// `wanted` is the digest `declared_identity().digest()` returns for the "
"product\n"
"// you intend — the same value `shacl explain` prints. `admit_expecting` "
"and\n"
"// `rebuild_expecting` check it FIRST, ahead of everything else either "
"restore\n"
"// seam checks, so the choice of repair strategy never bypasses the "
"binding.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 或者说明本意所指的究竟是哪个产物，并在不是该产物时按失败即关闭（fail "
"closed）处理。\n"
"// `wanted` 是 `declared_identity().digest()` 为目标产物返回的摘要\n"
"// ——与 `shacl explain` 打印的值相同。`admit_expecting` 与\n"
"// `rebuild_expecting` 会最先检查它，先于任一恢复扩展点所检查的\n"
"// 其他一切，因此修复策略的选择绝不会绕过该绑定。\n"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:486
msgid ""
"`ShapesProduct::open` runs the container's cheap integrity tier — magic, "
"format version, section directory, canonical offsets, zero padding, every "
"section's SHA-256, the identity region, the trailer, the whole-container "
"digest — and admits nothing. Holding the resulting view is a statement about "
"framing, never about fitness, which is exactly what makes reading a refused "
"product's declared identity useful."
msgstr ""
"`ShapesProduct::open` 运行容器的低成本完整性层级——魔数、格式版本、部分目录、"
"规范化偏移量、零填充、每个部分的 SHA-256、身份区域、尾部、整个容器的摘要——并"
"且不准入任何内容。持有所得的视图只是关于封装结构（framing）的陈述，从不是关于"
"适用性的陈述，而这正是读取被拒绝产物所声明的身份之所以有用的原因。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:493
msgid "Host-injected implementations"
msgstr "宿主注入的实现"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:495
msgid ""
"Everything above passes `HostBindings::empty()`, which is what a product of "
"`ShapesProfile::CORE` needs: every capability such a product exercises is "
"declared by the shapes graph itself. A Rust host may still wire native "
"SPARQL functions or custom aggregates of its own, and when it does, the "
"product binds **two** facts about that host rather than one:"
msgstr ""
"上文的一切都传入 `HostBindings::empty()`，这正是 `ShapesProfile::CORE` 产物所"
"需要的：此类产物所使用的每项能力都由形状图自身声明。Rust 宿主仍然可以接入自己"
"的原生 SPARQL 函数或自定义聚合，而当它这样做时，产物会绑定关于该宿主的**两项"
"**事实，而不是一项："

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:501
msgid ""
"the registries' **declarations** — each injected entry's IRI, arity and "
"volatility — which is all a fingerprint reproducible in another process can "
"ever cover; and"
msgstr ""
"注册表的**声明**——每个注入条目的 IRI、元数与易变性——这是在另一个进程中可复现"
"的指纹所能涵盖的全部内容；以及"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:504
msgid ""
"an **implementation identity**: an opaque byte string the caller uses to "
"name the build those declarations resolve to, such as a release version or a "
"commit digest."
msgstr ""
"一个**实现身份**：调用方用来指明这些声明所解析到的构建的不透明字节串，例如发"
"布版本或提交摘要。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:508
msgid ""
"The second is not belt-and-braces. Two builds of one host can register the "
"same IRI to two different closures that declare identical arity and "
"volatility and compute different answers — indistinguishable by every fact a "
"registry can state about itself. A binding over declarations alone would "
"admit a product prepared against one build under the other and validate "
"green, which is the silent wrong answer this codec exists to rule out."
msgstr ""
"第二项并非多此一举。同一宿主的两个构建可以把同一个 IRI 注册到两个不同的闭包"
"上，二者声明完全相同的元数与易变性，却计算出不同的答案——从注册表所能陈述的关"
"于自身的每项事实来看都无法区分。仅基于声明的绑定会在另一个构建下准入针对某一"
"构建预备的产物，并给出通过（绿色）的验证结果，而这正是该编解码器所要排除的静"
"默错误答案。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:515
msgid ""
"So a preparation whose injected population is not empty **cannot be packed "
"without an identity at all**: the writer refuses on `unsupported-capability` "
"rather than emitting a product whose host half nothing could check. And a "
"restore that supplies the same declarations under a different identity is "
"refused on the registry dimension that carries it."
msgstr ""
"因此，注入集合非空的预备结果**完全不带身份时无法打包**：写出器会以 "
"`unsupported-capability` 拒绝，而不是输出一个其宿主那一半无法被任何东西检查的"
"产物。而在不同身份下提供相同声明的恢复，会在承载该身份的注册表维度上被拒绝。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:525
msgid ""
"// The byte string that tells this build of the host's natives apart from "
"every\n"
"// other build of them. PurRDF never interprets it.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 用于把宿主原生实现的这一构建与其所有其他构建区分开来的\n"
"// 字节串。PurRDF 从不解释它。\n"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:528
msgid "b\"example.org/host@1\""
msgstr "b\"example.org/host@1\""

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:529
msgid "// `prepared` carries the host's natives in `Shapes::functions`.\n"
msgstr "// `prepared` 在 `Shapes::functions` 中携带宿主的原生实现。\n"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:532
msgid ""
"// ...and the restore names the same build, beside the registries it wires.\n"
msgstr "// ……而恢复在其所接入的注册表旁指明同一个构建。\n"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:543
msgid ""
"What the mechanism does not do is verify the identity. PurRDF cannot read a "
"host's machine code and confirm the bytes name it; the identity is the "
"caller's claim about its own build, and what the codec enforces is that a "
"restore claiming a _different_ one stops at the boundary. A host that spells "
"two different builds with one identity has told the binding they are the "
"same build."
msgstr ""
"该机制不做的是验证身份。PurRDF 无法读取宿主的机器码并确认这些字节指明的就是"
"它；身份是调用方关于其自身构建的声称，编解码器所强制的是：声称*不同*身份的恢"
"复会在边界处停止。用同一个身份拼写两个不同构建的宿主，等于告诉了绑定它们是同"
"一个构建。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:549
msgid ""
"An absent identity is the empty byte string, and it encodes as nothing at "
"all: the three host rows stay the bare declaration fingerprints. That is why "
"a product with nothing injected — which is every product the paths above "
"write — is byte-identical to what a build that had never heard of "
"implementation identities would produce."
msgstr ""
"缺失的身份是空字节串，并且编码后不占任何内容：三个宿主行仍然只是单纯的声明指"
"纹。正因如此，未注入任何内容的产物——也就是上述路径写出的每个产物——与一个从未"
"听说过实现身份的构建所产生的结果逐字节相同。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:555
msgid "Corroborating a product"
msgstr "佐证产物"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:562
msgid ""
"`verify` is the codec's **cold** path and is deliberately not reachable from "
"a restore. It re-canonicalizes the shapes graph's blank nodes and compares "
"the result against the digest the product's identity claims — a graph-"
"isomorphism computation that can cost more than the shapes parse a product "
"exists to eliminate. Call it from a build step, a release check or a "
"conformance harness; never before every validation."
msgstr ""
"`verify` 是编解码器的**冷**路径，并且有意设计为无法从恢复中到达。它对形状图的"
"空节点重新规范化，并将结果与产物身份所声称的摘要进行比较——这是一种图同构计"
"算，其开销可能超过产物本来要消除的形状解析开销。应在构建步骤、发布检查或一致"
"性测试框架中调用它；绝不要在每次验证之前调用。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:569
msgid ""
"What `admit` establishes about the dataset is that the section is the one "
"the container sealed — the per-section SHA-256 and the whole-container "
"digest both cover its bytes, so a swapped section is refused. What only "
"`verify` establishes is that those bytes _canonicalize_ to the digest the "
"identity records. A product whose stored canonical digest has been tampered "
"with will open, will admit, and will fail `verify`; that split is pinned by "
"test and is not an accident of layering."
msgstr ""
"`admit` 就数据集所确立的是：该部分正是容器所封存的那一个——按部分计算的 "
"SHA-256 与整个容器的摘要都覆盖其字节，因此被替换的部分会被拒绝。只有 "
"`verify` 才能确立的是：这些字节*规范化*后得到身份所记录的摘要。一个存储的规范"
"化摘要被篡改过的产物能够打开，能够准入，而会在 `verify` 中失败；这种划分由测"
"试固定，并非分层带来的偶然结果。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:577
msgid ""
"It prints the product's 64-character lowercase-hex identity digest on stdout "
"and exits `0`. A refusal names its dimension on stderr and exits `1`."
msgstr ""
"它在 stdout 上打印产物的 64 个字符的小写十六进制身份摘要，并以 `0` 退出。拒绝"
"会在 stderr 上指明其维度，并以 `1` 退出。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:580
msgid "Reading a product without admitting it"
msgstr "读取产物而不准入它"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:582
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ purrdf shacl explain shapes.purrshp\n"
"format-version 1\n"
"stage-id 7416f78d…\n"
"stage-known true\n"
"identity-digest 9f2c…\n"
"identity-components 11\n"
"identity source-dataset 0x1f0a…\n"
"identity shapes-graph \"(present) https://example.org/shapes\"\n"
"identity doc-prefixes 0x02657808…\n"
"identity base \"(present) https://example.org/shapes\"\n"
"identity profile \"purrdf-shacl-core-v1\"\n"
"identity box-role-vocab 0x00\n"
"identity user-functions-declared 0x4c1d…\n"
"identity user-functions-injected 0x4c1d…\n"
"identity aggregate-registry 0xb7e0…\n"
"identity property-function-registry 0xb7e0…\n"
"identity class-catalog 0x63aa…\n"
"parse-base https://example.org/shapes\n"
"parse-shapes-graph https://example.org/shapes\n"
"parse-prefixes 3\n"
"parse-prefix ex https://example.org/\n"
"parse-prefix sh http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#\n"
"parse-prefix xsd http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```console\n"
"$ purrdf shacl explain shapes.purrshp\n"
"format-version 1\n"
"stage-id 7416f78d…\n"
"stage-known true\n"
"identity-digest 9f2c…\n"
"identity-components 11\n"
"identity source-dataset 0x1f0a…\n"
"identity shapes-graph \"(present) https://example.org/shapes\"\n"
"identity doc-prefixes 0x02657808…\n"
"identity base \"(present) https://example.org/shapes\"\n"
"identity profile \"purrdf-shacl-core-v1\"\n"
"identity box-role-vocab 0x00\n"
"identity user-functions-declared 0x4c1d…\n"
"identity user-functions-injected 0x4c1d…\n"
"identity aggregate-registry 0xb7e0…\n"
"identity property-function-registry 0xb7e0…\n"
"identity class-catalog 0x63aa…\n"
"parse-base https://example.org/shapes\n"
"parse-shapes-graph https://example.org/shapes\n"
"parse-prefixes 3\n"
"parse-prefix ex https://example.org/\n"
"parse-prefix sh http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#\n"
"parse-prefix xsd http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#\n"
"```"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:608
msgid ""
"Deterministic `key value` lines in a fixed order, terminated by a newline, "
"so a consumer can split on whitespace without a parser. An identity "
"component's value is rendered as `\"text\"` when it is printable UTF-8 and "
"`0x…` lowercase hex otherwise."
msgstr ""
"按固定顺序输出的确定性 `key value` 行，以换行符结尾，因此使用方无须解析器即可"
"按空白切分。身份组成项的值在其为可打印 UTF-8 时呈现为 `\"text\"`，否则呈现为 "
"`0x…` 小写十六进制。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:613
msgid ""
"`stage-known` is the fact to act on: `false` says this build's `admit` will "
"refuse these bytes and `rebuild` is the path that still restores them."
msgstr ""
"`stage-known` 是据以行动的事实：`false` 表示本构建的 `admit` 会拒绝这些字节，"
"而 `rebuild` 是仍能恢复它们的路径。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:616
msgid ""
"`identity box-role-vocab 0x00` above is the encoding of **absent** — the "
"product this example packed with no `--box-role-vocab`. A product packed "
"with the flag renders a longer `0x…` run instead (the six derived term IRIs, "
"length-prefixed and key-sorted), never `0x00`; the two are deliberately "
"distinguishable so a restore can never confuse \"the feature is inactive\" "
"with \"the feature is active over a vocabulary of empty IRIs\"."
msgstr ""
"上面的 `identity box-role-vocab 0x00` 是**缺失**的编码——该示例打包的产物没有"
"使用 `--box-role-vocab`。使用了该标志打包的产物会呈现一段更长的 `0x…`（六个推"
"导出的术语 IRI，带长度前缀并按键排序），绝不会是 `0x00`；二者有意设计为可区分"
"的，这样恢复就绝不会把「该功能未激活」与「该功能在一个由空 IRI 组成的词汇表上"
"激活」相混淆。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:623
msgid ""
"This is what makes a named refusal actionable rather than a log line. A "
"restore refused on `prefixes` is answered by reading which prefix map the "
"product actually carries and fixing the configuration — not by guessing, and "
"not by re-packing blindly. Comparing that answer across **two** products — "
"the one you have and the one you meant — is [`shacl diff`](#comparing-two-"
"products), rather than running `explain` twice and comparing the rendering "
"by eye."
msgstr ""
"正是这一点使具名拒绝成为可据以行动的信息，而不只是一行日志。在 `prefixes` 上"
"被拒绝的恢复，应通过读取产物实际携带的是哪个前缀映射并修正配置来应对——而不是"
"靠猜测，也不是盲目地重新打包。在**两个**产物之间——手头的那个与本意所指的那个"
"——比较这一答案，用的是 [`shacl diff`](#比较两个产物)，而不是运行两次 "
"`explain` 再用肉眼比较呈现结果。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:630
msgid "Comparing two products"
msgstr "比较两个产物"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:638
msgid ""
"`shacl diff` opens **both** products WITHOUT admitting either — the same "
"framing-and-integrity-only tier `shacl explain` reads through — and prints "
"every identity component whose value differs, one `diff <label> <value-in-a> "
"<value-in-b>` line per component, in `A`'s own component order. `diff-count "
"0` and no `diff` lines means the two products declared identical identities."
msgstr ""
"`shacl diff` 打开**两个**产物，但**不**准入其中任何一个——与 `shacl explain` "
"读取时所用的同一个仅限封装结构与完整性的层级——并打印每个值不同的身份组成项，"
"每个组成项一行 `diff <label> <value-in-a> <value-in-b>`，按 `A` 自身的组成项"
"顺序排列。`diff-count 0` 且没有 `diff` 行，表示两个产物声明了完全相同的身份。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:644
msgid ""
"This is what makes a NAMED refusal actionable between two artifacts rather "
"than just one. `shacl explain` answers \"what does THIS product say it was "
"compiled from\"; before `diff` existed, an operator whose restore was "
"refused on a named dimension had to run `explain` twice — on the product in "
"hand and on the one they meant to restore — and compare the rendering by eye "
"to find which declaration moved. `diff` is that comparison, done once, over "
"the identical decoded components `explain` renders, so the two can never "
"disagree about what a component's value is."
msgstr ""
"正是这一点使**具名**拒绝在两个工件之间、而不只是在一个工件上成为可据以行动的"
"信息。`shacl explain` 回答的是「**这个**产物声称自己是由什么编译而来的」；在 "
"`diff` 出现之前，恢复在某个具名维度上被拒绝的操作人员必须运行两次 `explain`——"
"一次针对手头的产物，一次针对本想恢复的产物——并用肉眼比较呈现结果，以找出是哪"
"项声明发生了变动。`diff` 就是这一比较，一次完成，作用于 `explain` 所呈现的完"
"全相同的已解码组成项，因此二者在某个组成项的值是什么这一点上永远不会出现分"
"歧。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:653
msgid ""
"Exit codes mirror `shacl verify`'s certified/refused split rather than "
"`validate`'s conforms/non-conforms one, because a `diff` that finds a "
"difference is a **decided answer about two artifacts**, not a validation "
"verdict about data: exit `0` when the two identities are identical, exit `1` "
"when they differ (the difference is printed on stdout either way), and exit "
"`2` for a usage error."
msgstr ""
"退出码沿用 `shacl verify` 的已认证/已拒绝划分，而不是 `validate` 的符合/不符"
"合划分，因为发现差异的 `diff` 是一个**关于两个工件的已判定答案**，而不是关于"
"数据的验证裁决：两个身份完全相同时以 `0` 退出，不同时以 `1` 退出（无论哪种情"
"况，差异都打印在 stdout 上），用法错误时以 `2` 退出。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:660
msgid ""
"`diff` never admits either side, so it works on a product whose preparation "
"stage id this build does not recognize — the stage id lives in the product's "
"separate preparation memo, not in the identity `diff` compares, and is "
"exactly the situation an operator reaches for a diff to make sense of: "
"\"`validate --shapes-product` refuses this file outright; what, concretely, "
"would change if I re-packed it?\""
msgstr ""
"`diff` 从不准入任何一方，因此它也适用于预备阶段 id 不为本构建所识别的产物——阶"
"段 id 存放在产物单独的预备备忘中，而不在 `diff` 所比较的身份中，而这恰恰是操"
"作人员求助于 diff 来弄清楚的情形：「`validate --shapes-product` 直接拒绝了这"
"个文件；如果重新打包，具体会有什么变化？」"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:667
msgid "The refusal dimensions"
msgstr "拒绝维度"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:669
msgid ""
"Every refusal carries one of twenty stable kebab-case labels, printed to "
"stderr as `shacl dimension <label>`. **The dimension is what you branch on; "
"the message is what you read.** Matching on message text is not supported."
msgstr ""
"每次拒绝都带有二十个稳定的 kebab-case 标签之一，以 `shacl dimension <label>` "
"的形式打印到 stderr。**据以分支的是维度；供人阅读的是消息。** 不支持按消息文"
"本进行匹配。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:673
msgid ""
"The dimensions are checked from the outside of the container inward, and the "
"first one that fails is the one reported — so the label always names the "
"outermost unmet precondition rather than a downstream symptom of it."
msgstr ""
"各维度由容器外层向内依次检查，第一个失败的维度就是被报告的维度——因此标签总是"
"指明最外层未满足的前提条件，而不是其下游症状。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:677
msgid ""
"The twenty split into two groups by **which verb can report them**, and the "
"split is not a taxonomy: it is the cost decision this codec is built around. "
"A restore is the common path and must not canonicalize a shapes graph's "
"blank nodes; certification is the cold path that does. A dimension only one "
"of the two can reach is not something the other quietly skips — it is a "
"statement that verb never makes."
msgstr ""
"这二十个维度按**哪个动词能够报告它们**分为两组，而这种划分并非分类学：它是该"
"编解码器所围绕的成本决策。恢复是常用路径，不得对形状图的空节点进行规范化；认"
"证是会进行规范化的冷路径。只有两者之一能够到达的维度，并不是另一方悄悄跳过的"
"东西——而是表明该动词从不作出这一陈述。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:684
msgid "Admit-time dimensions"
msgstr "准入时维度"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:686
msgid ""
"Reported by `validate --shapes-product` on every restore, by `shacl explain` "
"for the structural rows it reaches while opening the bytes, and by `shacl "
"verify`, which opens the product before it certifies anything."
msgstr ""
"由 `validate --shapes-product` 在每次恢复时报告；由 `shacl explain` 报告其在"
"打开字节时所到达的结构性各行；由 `shacl verify` 报告，因为它在认证任何内容之"
"前会先打开产物。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:690 src/validation/shapes-products.md:719
