"the two identities differ (the `diff` lines are still printed, on stdout)"
msgstr "两个身份不同（`diff` 行仍会打印在 stdout 上）"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:750
msgid "bad flags, or both `A` and `B` naming standard input"
msgstr "错误的标志，或 `A` 与 `B` 都指定为标准输入"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:751
msgid ""
"`purrdf validate --shapes-product FILE [--rebuild] [--expect-identity HEX] "
"[IN]`"
msgstr ""
"`purrdf validate --shapes-product FILE [--rebuild] [--expect-identity HEX] "
"[IN]`"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:751
msgid ""
"restore and validate — `--rebuild` re-derives from the carried dataset "
"instead of admitting the memo"
msgstr "恢复并验证——`--rebuild` 从所携带的数据集重新推导，而不是准入备忘"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:751
msgid "validation ran"
msgstr "验证已运行"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:751
msgid "product refused"
msgstr "产物被拒绝"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:751
msgid ""
"bad flags, a parse flag passed against a product, `--rebuild` or `--expect-"
"identity` without a product, or an `--expect-identity` that is not 64 "
"hexadecimal digits"
msgstr ""
"错误的标志、对产物传入了解析标志、在没有产物时使用 `--rebuild` 或 `--expect-"
"identity`，或 `--expect-identity` 的值不是 64 个十六进制数字"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:753
msgid ""
"`IN` defaults to `-` (standard input) for `verify` and `explain`. For "
"`validate`, `--shapes-product -` collides with the data graph's own default "
"of `-` and is refused by name: there is only one standard input. `diff`'s "
"two products, `A` and `B`, are both required positional paths with no "
"default, for the identical reason: naming standard input for both would give "
"each product part of one byte stream."
msgstr ""
"对于 `verify` 与 `explain`，`IN` 默认为 `-`（标准输入）。对于 `validate`，`--"
"shapes-product -` 会与数据图自身的默认值 `-` 冲突，因而被点名拒绝：标准输入只"
"有一个。`diff` 的两个产物 `A` 与 `B` 都是必需的位置路径，没有默认值，原因完全"
"相同：把两者都指定为标准输入，会使每个产物各得到同一字节流的一部分。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:760
msgid ""
"`validate --shapes FILE [--box-role-vocab NS]` accepts the identical flag on "
"the parse lane — see [Producing a product](#producing-a-product) above — and "
"refuses it by name against `--shapes-product`, in the four-flag table above."
msgstr ""
"`validate --shapes FILE [--box-role-vocab NS]` 在解析通道上接受完全相同的标志"
"——参见上文的[生成产物](#生成产物)——并在与 `--shapes-product` 同用时点名拒绝"
"它，见上面的四标志表。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:764
msgid ""
"`validate` additionally exits `3` when a governor budget trips, and always "
"writes `shacl shapes-provenance <token>` before the run and `shacl conforms "
"true` or `shacl conforms false` plus `shacl results <N>` after it, all on "
"stderr — including when the shapes came from a product."
msgstr ""
"`validate` 在 governor（执行调控器）预算触发时还会以 `3` 退出，并且总是在运行"
"之前写出 `shacl shapes-provenance <token>`，在运行之后写出 `shacl conforms "
"true` 或 `shacl conforms false` 以及 `shacl results <N>`，全部输出到 stderr——"
"包括形状来自产物的情况。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:775
msgid "# bytes, byte-deterministic\n"
msgstr "# 字节，逐字节确定性\n"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:777
msgid "# framing and integrity only\n"
msgstr "# 仅限封装结构与完整性\n"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:778
msgid "# 1\n"
msgstr "# 1\n"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:779
msgid "# True\n"
msgstr "# True\n"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:780
msgid "# 64 lowercase hex characters\n"
msgstr "# 64 个小写十六进制字符\n"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:787
msgid ""
"# Which artifact did that verdict come out of? Total — always an answer, "
"never\n"
"# \"unknown\": \"parsed\", \"restored-admitted <digest>\" or \"restored-"
"rebuilt <digest>\".\n"
msgstr ""
"# 该裁决出自哪个工件？完全的（total）——总有答案，绝不会是\n"
"# \"unknown\"：\"parsed\"、\"restored-admitted <digest>\" 或 \"restored-"
"rebuilt <digest>\"。\n"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:790
msgid "# restored-admitted 9f2c…1b\n"
msgstr "# restored-admitted 9f2c…1b\n"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:791
msgid ""
"# …or say which product you meant, and fail closed when it is not that one.\n"
msgstr ""
"# ……或者说明本意所指的是哪个产物，并在不是该产物时按失败即关闭（fail closed）"
"处理。\n"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:793 src/validation/shapes-products.md:797
msgid "\"9f2c…64 lowercase hex…1b\""
msgstr "\"9f2c…64 lowercase hex…1b\""

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:794
msgid ""
"# The same binding, over the rebuild seam: the expectation is checked "
"FIRST,\n"
"# ahead of the re-derivation, so choosing to rebuild never bypasses it.\n"
msgstr ""
"# 同一绑定，经由重建扩展点：期望会最先检查，\n"
"# 先于重新推导，因此选择重建绝不会绕过它。\n"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:800
msgid ""
"`PreparedShapes.provenance()` is the Python spelling of the CLI's `shacl "
"shapes-provenance` receipt, and renders the identical token — the digest in "
"it is the value `identity_digest()` reports, so it can be handed straight "
"back to `admit_expecting()`. A preparation built by `Shapes(...).prepare()` "
"answers `parsed`, because it was never restored from an artifact and none "
"may be invented for it."
msgstr ""
"`PreparedShapes.provenance()` 是 CLI 的 `shacl shapes-provenance` 回执在 "
"Python 中的写法，呈现完全相同的标记——其中的摘要就是 `identity_digest()` 所报"
"告的值，因此可以直接回传给 `admit_expecting()`。由 `Shapes(...).prepare()` 构"
"建的预备结果回答 `parsed`，因为它从未从工件中恢复过，也不得为它虚构任何工件。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:807
msgid ""
"`ShapesProduct.certify()` is the cold path; call it from a build step or a "
"test. Refusals raise `shapes.ShapesProductError`, whose `.dimension` carries "
"the label string (or `None` when no product was ever inspected)."
msgstr ""
"`ShapesProduct.certify()` 是冷路径；应从构建步骤或测试中调用它。拒绝会抛出 "
"`shapes.ShapesProductError`，其 `.dimension` 携带标签字符串（从未检查过任何产"
"物时为 `None`）。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:811
msgid ""
"The submodule is `purrdf.shapes`. `purrdf.shacl` is a back-compatible alias "
"for the same object and keeps working, but new code should spell the "
"canonical name: the alias predates the surface this page describes, and the "
"two names resolving to one module is the kind of thing that reads as two "
"APIs to someone learning it."
msgstr ""
"子模块是 `purrdf.shapes`。`purrdf.shacl` 是同一对象的向后兼容别名，仍然可用，"
"但新代码应写规范名称：该别名早于本页所描述的接口，而两个名称解析到同一个模"
"块，在学习者看来就像是两套 API。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:816
msgid ""
"`admit_expecting(expected_identity)` is `admit()` bound to the product you "
"meant: it takes the 64 hexadecimal digits `identity_digest()` reports, and "
"raises `ShapesProductError` with `.dimension == \"shapes-graph\"` when the "
"product carries a different binding. A selector that is not a digest raises "
"a plain `ValueError` instead — no product was opened, so nothing may be "
"blamed on one."
msgstr ""
"`admit_expecting(expected_identity)` 是绑定到本意所指产物的 `admit()`：它接"
"受 `identity_digest()` 所报告的 64 个十六进制数字，当产物携带不同的绑定时，抛"
"出 `.dimension == \"shapes-graph\"` 的 `ShapesProductError`。不是摘要的选择器"
"则会抛出普通的 `ValueError`——没有打开任何产物，因此不能把责任归到某个产物上。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:822
msgid ""
"`rebuild()` re-derives from the SAME carried dataset `admit()` restores a "
"memo of, so calling it on a CURRENT product (`stage_known() == True`) "
"reaches the byte-identical report — it is a second door onto one product, "
"never a second, divergent answer. `rebuild_expecting(expected_identity)` is "
"its bound twin, taking the identical `expected_identity` `admit_expecting` "
"does: the expectation is checked FIRST, ahead of the re-derivation, exactly "
"as it is on `admit_expecting`, so a caller who reaches for the forward-"
"compatibility rescue never loses the binding."
msgstr ""
"`rebuild()` 从 `admit()` 恢复其备忘的那个**同一**携带数据集重新推导，因此在**"
"当前**产物（`stage_known() == True`）上调用它会得到逐字节相同的报告——它是通往"
"同一产物的第二道门，绝不是第二个、有分歧的答案。"
"`rebuild_expecting(expected_identity)` 是它的绑定孪生版本，接受与 "
"`admit_expecting` 完全相同的 `expected_identity`：期望会**最先**检查，先于重"
"新推导，与 `admit_expecting` 上完全一样，因此求助于前向兼容挽救手段的调用方绝"
"不会失去绑定。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:831
msgid "From JavaScript / WebAssembly"
msgstr "在 JavaScript / WebAssembly 中"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:853
msgid ""
"// …or, for a stage id this guest does not know, re-derive from the carried\n"
"  // dataset instead of admitting the memo — the remedy the `stage-id` "
"refusal\n"
"  // above would name.\n"
msgstr ""
"// ……或者，对于本客体（guest）不认识的阶段 id，从所携带的\n"
"  // 数据集重新推导，而不是准入备忘——即上文 `stage-id` 拒绝\n"
"  // 所会指明的补救手段。\n"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:858
msgid ""
"// …or say which product you meant, and fail closed when it is not that "
"one.\n"
msgstr ""
"// ……或者说明本意所指的是哪个产物，并在不是该产物时按失败即关闭（fail "
"closed）处理。\n"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:861
msgid ""
"// …or both: rebuild AND fail closed when it is not the product you meant.\n"
"  // The expectation is checked FIRST, ahead of the re-derivation, so the\n"
"  // rescue never bypasses the binding.\n"
msgstr ""
"// ……或者两者兼用：重建，并且在不是本意所指的产物时按失败即关闭处理。\n"
"  // 期望会最先检查，先于重新推导，因此\n"
"  // 挽救手段绝不会绕过绑定。\n"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:875
msgid ""
"A wasm guest has no retrieval IRI to derive a base from, so the host "
"supplies `shapesBase` explicitly; it is recorded in the product, and a "
"restore resolves the same relative references without the document."
msgstr ""
"wasm 客体（guest）没有可从中推导基准的检索 IRI，因此由宿主显式提供 "
"`shapesBase`；它会记录在产物中，恢复时无须该文档即可解析同样的相对引用。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:879
msgid ""
"`shaclProductValidateToSarifRebuild` re-derives from the SAME carried "
"dataset `shaclProductValidateToSarif` restores a memo of, so calling it on a "
"CURRENT product reaches the byte-identical report — it is a second door onto "
"one product, never a second, divergent answer. "
"`shaclProductValidateToSarifRebuildExpecting` is its bound twin, taking the "
"identical `expectIdentity` `shaclProductValidateToSarifExpecting` does: the "
"expectation is checked FIRST, ahead of the re-derivation, exactly as it is "
"on `shaclProductValidateToSarifExpecting`, so a host that reaches for the "
"forward-compatibility rescue never loses the binding."
msgstr ""
"`shaclProductValidateToSarifRebuild` 从 `shaclProductValidateToSarif` 恢复其"
"备忘的那个**同一**携带数据集重新推导，因此在**当前**产物上调用它会得到逐字节"
"相同的报告——它是通往同一产物的第二道门，绝不是第二个、有分歧的答案。"
"`shaclProductValidateToSarifRebuildExpecting` 是它的绑定孪生版本，接受与 "
"`shaclProductValidateToSarifExpecting` 完全相同的 `expectIdentity`：期望会**"
"最先**检查，先于重新推导，与 `shaclProductValidateToSarifExpecting` 上完全一"
"样，因此求助于前向兼容挽救手段的宿主绝不会失去绑定。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:889
msgid ""
"`shaclProductValidateToSarifExpecting` takes the 64 hexadecimal digits "
"`shaclProductExplain` prints on its `identity-digest` line. A product "
"carrying a different binding rejects with `dimension === \"shapes-graph\"`; "
"a selector that is not a digest rejects with `dimension === undefined`, "
"because no product was inspected. "
"`shaclProductValidateToSarifRebuildExpecting` carries the identical selector "
"and the identical refusal shape."
msgstr ""
"`shaclProductValidateToSarifExpecting` 接受 `shaclProductExplain` 在其 "
"`identity-digest` 行上打印的 64 个十六进制数字。携带不同绑定的产物会以 "
"`dimension === \"shapes-graph\"` 拒绝；不是摘要的选择器会以 `dimension === "
"undefined` 拒绝，因为没有检查任何产物。"
"`shaclProductValidateToSarifRebuildExpecting` 采用完全相同的选择器与完全相同"
"的拒绝形式。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:896
msgid "From C"
msgstr "在 C 中"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:898
msgid ""
"The C ABI exposes `purrdf_shapes_product_encode`, "
"`purrdf_shapes_product_open`, `purrdf_shapes_product_admit`, "
"`purrdf_shapes_product_admit_expecting`, `purrdf_shapes_product_rebuild`, "
"`purrdf_shapes_product_rebuild_expecting` and "
"`purrdf_shapes_product_certify`, with "
"`purrdf_shapes_product_error_dimension` returning the refusal's stable label "
"(or `NULL` when the shapes document simply did not parse)."
msgstr ""
"C ABI 公开了 `purrdf_shapes_product_encode`、`purrdf_shapes_product_open`、"
"`purrdf_shapes_product_admit`、`purrdf_shapes_product_admit_expecting`、"
"`purrdf_shapes_product_rebuild`、`purrdf_shapes_product_rebuild_expecting` "
"与 `purrdf_shapes_product_certify`，并由 "
"`purrdf_shapes_product_error_dimension` 返回拒绝的稳定标签（形状文档只是未能"
"解析时返回 `NULL`）。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:905
msgid ""
"`purrdf_shapes_product_rebuild` is the forward-compatibility twin of "
"`purrdf_shapes_product_admit`: it re-derives the preparation from the shapes "
"dataset the product carries instead of admitting its memo, which is the "
"remedy `purrdf_shapes_product_admit`'s `stage-id` refusal names. "
"`purrdf_shapes_product_rebuild_expecting` is its bound twin, taking the "
"identical `expect_identity` `purrdf_shapes_product_admit_expecting` does: "
"the expectation is checked FIRST, ahead of the re-derivation, exactly as it "
"is on `purrdf_shapes_product_admit_expecting`, so a C host that reaches for "
"the forward-compatibility rescue never loses the binding."
msgstr ""
"`purrdf_shapes_product_rebuild` 是 `purrdf_shapes_product_admit` 的前向兼容孪"
"生版本：它从产物所携带的形状数据集重新推导预备结果，而不是准入其备忘，这正是 "
"`purrdf_shapes_product_admit` 的 `stage-id` 拒绝所指明的补救手段。"
"`purrdf_shapes_product_rebuild_expecting` 是它的绑定孪生版本，接受与 "
"`purrdf_shapes_product_admit_expecting` 完全相同的 `expect_identity`：期望会"
"**最先**检查，先于重新推导，与 `purrdf_shapes_product_admit_expecting` 上完全"
"一样，因此求助于前向兼容挽救手段的 C 宿主绝不会失去绑定。"

#: src/validation/shapes-products.md:915
msgid ""
"`purrdf_shapes_product_admit_expecting` is `purrdf_shapes_product_admit` "
"bound to the product you meant: it takes the `identity-digest` value "
"`purrdf_shapes_product_open` renders, as a NUL-terminated C string, and "
"returns `PURRDF_STATUS_SHAPES_PRODUCT_ERROR` with the dimension `shapes-"
"graph` when the product carries a different binding. A selector that is not "
"64 hexadecimal digits returns `PURRDF_STATUS_INVALID_ARGUMENT` and no "
"dimension. `purrdf_shapes_product_rebuild_expecting` carries the identical "
"selector and the identical refusal shape. See [`crates/rdf-capi/include/"
"purrdf.h`](https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf/blob/main/crates/"
"rdf-capi/include/purrdf.h) and [Getting Started: C](../getting-started/c.md)."
msgstr ""
"`purrdf_shapes_product_admit_expecting` 是绑定到本意所指产物的 "
"`purrdf_shapes_product_admit`：它接受 `purrdf_shapes_product_open` 所呈现的 "
"`identity-digest` 值（以 NUL 结尾的 C 字符串），当产物携带不同的绑定时，返回 "
"`PURRDF_STATUS_SHAPES_PRODUCT_ERROR` 以及维度 `shapes-graph`。不是 64 个十六"
"进制数字的选择器返回 `PURRDF_STATUS_INVALID_ARGUMENT`，且不带维度。"
"`purrdf_shapes_product_rebuild_expecting` 采用完全相同的选择器与完全相同的拒"
"绝形式。参见 [`crates/rdf-capi/include/purrdf.h`](https://github.com/"
"Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf/blob/main/crates/rdf-capi/include/purrdf.h) 与[入"
"门：C](../getting-started/c.md)。"

