#: src/entailment.md:100
msgid ""
"Two things differ from the materializing table above, and both are "
"consequences of the question rather than of any host:"
msgstr "与上面的物化表相比有两点不同，二者都源于所提出的问题，而非任何宿主："

#: src/entailment.md:103
msgid ""
"**Five regimes, not seven.** `owl-direct` is directed by a _query's_ class "
"expressions and `rif` entails under the _caller's_ rule document, and "
"\"premise, conclusion, regime\" carries neither. Both are refused by name on "
"every host — never answered under a weaker regime and labelled with the one "
"that was asked for — and both still materialize."
msgstr ""
"**五种机制，而不是七种。** `owl-direct` 由*查询*的类表达式引导，`rif` 在*调用"
"方*的规则文档下进行蕴涵，而「前提、结论、机制」两者都不携带。二者在每个宿主上"
"都会被点名拒绝——绝不会在较弱的机制下作答并贴上所请求机制的标签——而二者仍然可"
"以物化。"

#: src/entailment.md:108
msgid ""
"**The import table is a parameter, on every host.** An ontology's imports "
"closure _is_ the ontology, so a premise carrying an `owl:imports` the call "
"was not handed is a different premise. PurRDF fetches nothing, so the "
"closure arrives as caller-supplied configuration: an ordered list of "
"`(ontology IRI, document)` pairs, spelled `--import IRI=FILE` on the command "
"line. An import needs no pair when it names the premise document itself — "
"the CLI's `file://` retrieval IRI or `--base`, and on the Python, "
"WebAssembly and C hosts the `premise_iris` argument (`premiseIris` in "
"JavaScript), the IRIs the caller read the premise from, `[]` for bare text — "
"or an ontology the premise already holds (`<X> a owl:Ontology`, or an "
"`owl:versionIRI` naming it). Any other unresolved import is a refusal naming "
"the document, never a silently truncated premise."
msgstr ""
"**导入表在每个宿主上都是参数。** 本体的导入闭包*就是*该本体，因此，若前提携带"
"了一条调用方没有交给本次调用的 `owl:imports`，它就已是另一个前提。PurRDF 不获"
"取任何内容，因此导入闭包以调用方提供的配置形式到达：一个有序的 `(本体 IRI, 文"
"档)` 配对列表，在命令行上写作 `--import IRI=FILE`。当某个导入指向前提文档本身"
"时无需配对——在 CLI 上是 `file://` 获取 IRI 或 `--base`，在 Python、"
"WebAssembly 与 C 宿主上是 `premise_iris` 参数（JavaScript 中为 "
"`premiseIris`），即调用方读取前提所用的 IRI，裸文本则为 `[]`——或指向前提中已"
"有的本体（`<X> a owl:Ontology`，或某个 `owl:versionIRI` 指名它）时，同样无需"
"配对。其他任何未解析的导入都会以点名该文档的方式被拒绝，绝不会成为一个被静默"
"截断的前提。"

#: src/entailment.md:120
msgid ""
"A pattern is N-Triples with `?name` (or `$name`) in any position, the "
"**predicate** included. RDF reserves that position for an IRI, so the "
"boundary reaches it by rewriting each variable to a term drawn from a "
"namespace it has swept out of the caller's own text and mapping every "
"occurrence back afterwards; nothing of that namespace reaches a row, a "
"binding or a report. The one slot that admits no variable is a literal's "
"**datatype**: `\"5\"^^?d` asks for a binding in a position that holds an IRI "
"rather than a term, and it is refused by name — the stand-in must never be "
"left sitting there, matching the boundary's own namespace instead of the "
"caller's data. A predicate variable is projected like any other, and under "
"`owl-rl` it also renders a `limit`: it ranges over the whole predicate "
"vocabulary, so it ranges over the schema predicates, which the theorem "
"behind the rule table's completeness does not cover. That theorem is Theorem "
"PR1 of [OWL 2 Profiles §4.3](https://www.w3.org/TR/owl2-profiles/"
"#Reasoning_in_OWL_2_RL_and_RDF_Graphs_using_Rules), and its hypothesis has "
"two halves: the premise lies inside the OWL 2 RL syntax, and the conclusion "
"is _assertional_ — class assertions over class names, property assertions, "
"`owl:sameAs` and `owl:differentFrom` over named individuals. Only when both "
"hold is the rule table complete, so a schema conclusion is one the table "
"claims no completeness for, whether or not `scm-*` derives it. The predicate "
"variable also ranges over the constructs the mechanisms beyond the table "
"decide, for which the closure the rows are drawn from holds nothing."
msgstr "模式是在任意位置（包括**谓词**位置）带有 `?name`（或 `$name`）的 N-Triples。RDF 把该位置保留给 IRI，因此边界的做法是：把每个变量改写为取自某个命名空间的项（该命名空间由边界扫描调用方自己的文本后划出），之后再把每次出现映射回来；该命名空间的任何内容都不会出现在结果行、绑定或报告中。唯一不接受变量的位置是字面量的**数据类型**：`\"5\"^^?d` 要求在一个存放 IRI 而非项的位置上进行绑定，它会被点名拒绝——替身绝不能留在那里，否则它匹配的是边界自己的命名空间，而不是调用方的数据。谓词变量与其他变量一样被投影；在 `owl-rl` 下，它还会产生一个 `limit`：它的取值范围是整个谓词词汇表，因此也涵盖 schema 谓词，而规则表的完备性所依据的定理并不覆盖这些谓词。该定理是 [OWL 2 Profiles §4.3](https://www.w3.org/TR/owl2-profiles/#Reasoning_in_OWL_2_RL_and_RDF_Graphs_using_Rules) 中的定理 PR1，其假设分为两半：前提处于 OWL 2 RL 语法之内，且结论是*断言型*的——即基于类名的类断言、属性断言，以及基于具名个体的 `owl:sameAs` 与 `owl:differentFrom`。只有两半同时成立时规则表才是完备的，因此对于 schema 结论，无论 `scm-*` 是否推出了它，规则表都不声称完备。谓词变量还涵盖由规则表之外的判定手段所判定的构造，而结果行所取自的推理闭包对这些构造不含任何内容。"

#: src/entailment.md:142
msgid ""
"Every answer arrives with the certificate of the run underneath it — the "
"same `purrdf-reasoning-report` block a materialization renders, plus a "
"`mechanism` line naming which of the six reached the verdict."
msgstr ""
"每个答案都附带其背后那次运行的证书——与物化所输出的相同的 `purrdf-reasoning-"
"report` 块，外加一行 `mechanism`，指明是六种判定手段中的哪一种得出了裁决。"

